flowchart TB
  accTitle: Finite voltage descent and its recovery boundary
  accDescr: Every next probe lowers voltage. A floor, cached unsafe pair, failed candidate or Balanced efficiency wall ends only this sweep. Critical errors and user stops follow the run exit rules.
  INPUT([Start with a passing baseline or tier reference]) --> FLOOR["Choose the effective floor<br/>Explicit setting → model table → fallback<br/>Unknown model: 10% below starting voltage"]
  FLOOR --> NEXT{"A lower editable bin remains<br/>at or above the floor?"}
  NEXT -->|No| RETURN([Return the passing selection<br/>Continue to clock selection / final verification])
  NEXT -->|Yes| BUILD["Build the complete next curve<br/>Carry the requested MHz and measured upward gains<br/>Preserve the tier's tail policy"]
  BUILD --> CACHE{"Actual new voltage / clock<br/>blocked by the unsafe cache?"}
  CACHE -->|Yes| RETURN
  CACHE -->|No| PROBE["Reset → apply → verify readback → probe<br/>Q2RTX; CUDA when required by voltage band"]
  PROBE --> RESULT{"Probe outcome"}
  RESULT -->|Unsafe / ordinary rejection| RETURN
  RESULT -->|Pass| ACCEPT["Record exact passing evidence<br/>Update the selected curve and checkpoint"]
  ACCEPT --> WALL{"Balanced's confirmed FPS/W wall<br/>after the required voltage drop?"}
  WALL -->|Yes: retain the better point| RETURN
  WALL -->|No / other tier: descend again| NEXT
  RESULT -->|Critical failure| HALT([Stop probing; preserve completed profiles<br/>Exit handling in block 05])
  PROBE -.->|User stop| STOP([Stop request handling in block 05])
  classDef setup fill:#19334b,stroke:#84c7f5,color:#edf5fa,stroke-width:1.5px
  classDef work fill:#18382f,stroke:#80d9ac,color:#edf5fa,stroke-width:1.5px
  classDef gate fill:#302c20,stroke:#e9bd76,color:#fff0d8,stroke-width:1.5px
  classDef stop fill:#40252a,stroke:#ef9595,color:#fff0f0,stroke-width:1.5px
  class INPUT,FLOOR,BUILD,PROBE,ACCEPT,RETURN work
  class NEXT,CACHE,RESULT,WALL gate
  class HALT,STOP stop
